  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Which of the following numbers is prime?",
  "worked_solution": "A prime number is a positive whole number with exactly two distinct whole number factors: itself and $1.$\n\nThe only number that satisfies this definition is $19.$ It has only two factors: $1$ and $19.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}19 & =1\\times 19 \\\\  & =19\\times 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll the other given numbers have at least one factor distinct from itself, and $1:$\n\n- $15$ has $3$ and $5$ as factors:\n\n$$\n15=3\\times 5\n$$\n\n- $6$ has $2$ and $3$ as factors:\n\n$$\n6=2\\times 3\n$$\n\n- $8$ has $2$ and $4$ as factors:\n\n$$\n8=2\\times 4\n$$\n\n- $18$ has $2$ and $9$ as factors:\n\n$$\n18=2\\times 9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $19.$",
